# Quillon environment configuration.
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in values from your Vault.
# Every variable below is optional; set at least one provider key to run live.

# ---- Model providers (at least one enables live models) ----
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY alone routes to every upstream model.
# Names to set: OPENROUTER_API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY, CEREBRAS_API_KEY
# Optional OpenRouter overrides: OPENROUTER_BASE_URL, OPENROUTER_APP_NAME, APP_URL,
# OPENROUTER_STRUCTURED_OUTPUTS (set 0 only for a model that rejects json_schema)

# ---- Search / scraping / data providers ----
# Names to set: FIRECRAWL_API_KEY, EXA_API_KEY, APOLLO_API_KEY, BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY,
# APIFY_API_KEY, RAPIDAPI_KEY, SCRAPE_DO_API_KEY, KEENABLE_API_KEY,
# CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY, BROWSERLESS_TOKEN

# ---- Composio (MCP-style tool execution) ----
# Names to set: COMPOSIO_API_KEY, COMPOSIO_USER_ID

# ---- Cloudflare (R2 storage, DNS) ----
# Names to set: CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID,
# CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID, CLOUDFLARE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, CLOUDFLARE_R2_ENDPOINT

# ---- Single sign-on (Entra ID / any OIDC). Leave empty for local open mode. ----
# Names to set: AUTH_ISSUER, AUTH_CLIENT_ID, AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET

# ---- Governance ----
# Names to set: QUILLON_REQUIRE_AUTH, QUILLON_ADMIN_EMAILS, QUILLON_OPEN_MODE
#
# Capability grants are mandatory for member and viewer sessions; an
# administrator holds the whole platform. QUILLON_REQUIRE_GRANTS =1 forces them
# for admins too, =0 disables them, unset keeps the rule above.
# QUILLON_REQUIRE_GRANTS
#
# Tool authority: the manifest in src/lib/tool-manifest.ts decides every tool's
# class. QUILLON_TOOL_DENY="or_keys_*,cp_delete_*" blocks tools outright,
# QUILLON_TOOL_ADMIN_ALLOW names admin tools a member may still use, and
# QUILLON_TOOL_ALLOW_UNLISTED=1 (temporary only) lets unmanifested tools run.
# QUILLON_TOOL_DENY, QUILLON_TOOL_ADMIN_ALLOW, QUILLON_TOOL_ALLOW_UNLISTED
#
# MCP servers are administrator-only by default (their tools run third-party
# code). Name trusted servers — comma separated, exact names — to let members
# call their tools: QUILLON_MCP_MEMBER_SERVERS="github,linear".
# QUILLON_MCP_MEMBER_SERVERS
#
# Record-level restrictions: payroll, employee and finance records in
# Salesforce, HubSpot, NetSuite and Costpoint are administrator-only for writes.
# QUILLON_RECORD_ALLOW="netsuite:vendorpayment,salary" re-opens named records or
# fields for members.
# QUILLON_RECORD_ALLOW
#
# Audit checkpoints: QUILLON_AUDIT_KEY signs the audit head (keep it outside the
# database and back it up), QUILLON_AUDIT_SINK takes an https:// endpoint or an
# absolute path outside the workspace for each signed checkpoint.
# QUILLON_AUDIT_KEY, QUILLON_AUDIT_SINK
#
# Egress: QUILLON_EGRESS_ALLOWLIST restricts outbound hosts; an allowlisted host
# is still refused when it resolves to a private address unless the host is also
# in QUILLON_EGRESS_PRIVATE_HOSTS (deliberate internal services).
# QUILLON_EGRESS_ALLOWLIST, QUILLON_EGRESS_PRIVATE_HOSTS
#
# Sandbox: code execution requires a filesystem-isolating jail in production
# (bubblewrap, or chroot as a fallback). A network namespace alone ("netns")
# leaves the host filesystem readable and is refused, as is no isolation at all.
# QUILLON_SANDBOX_ALLOW_UNJAILED=1 only has effect outside production: it is a
# local-development convenience, never a production opt-out.
# QUILLON_SANDBOX_REQUIRE_ISOLATION=1 forces the requirement everywhere;
# QUILLON_SANDBOX_ALLOW_UNJAILED=1 (development only).
# QUILLON_SANDBOX_REQUIRE_ISOLATION, QUILLON_SANDBOX_ALLOW_UNJAILED
#
# Tenancy: memory, conversations, transactions, capability grants, durable runs,
# verification reports and the audit trail are scoped to the authenticated
# (tenant, owner) pair. The tenant comes from the session's organisation; rows
# written before this scoping existed carry the sentinel tenant "legacy" and are
# invisible to every identity.
#
# docker-compose.yml requires REDIS_PASSWORD and keeps Redis off the host network.
# REDIS_PASSWORD
